$info=bnzabros,bnzabrsj,
$bio

Bonanza Bros. (c) 1990 Sega.


Taking the roll of one of the two brothers, Robo and Mobo (or both, in two-player mode), players must make their way through a variety of scrolling platform levels and steal any loot they find, before making their way to the roof and escape in a waiting airship. Bonanza Bros. introuduced a true sense of 3D depth to the two-dimensional platform gameplay in that the enemy guards had a ''field-of-vision''; this made it possible for players to hide from the guards by ducking into alcoves, stairwells etc. Failure would see the brothers end up in jail.


The places the brothers burgle include a bank, a millionaire's mansion, a casino, a mint, an art gallery and a treasury.


