$info=gloc,glocr360,
$bio

G-Loc - Air Battle (c) 1990 Sega.


A direct sequel to 1987's "After Burner", G-loc adopts its predecessor's action-packed, if somewhat limited, gameplay. Most of the action is viewed from a first-person, in-cockpit view, but this occasionally switches to the familiar third-person perspective of After Burner. The object of the game is to shoot enemy planes as they approach from front and behind; rolling and swerving to avoid incoming enemy fire. The levels take the player through a variety of different landscapes, including wide plains and canyons.


