$info=lethalen,lethalej,
$bio

Lethal Enforcers (c) 1992 Konami.


As an undercover police officer the player's mission is to put a stop to an array of criminals ranging from bank robbers, hijackers and numerous other law breakers. As well as upholding the law, players must also try to protect innocent members of the public from the criminal gangs, being cafeful not to accidently shoot them. Shooting innocent victims will result in the player's energy level being severely reduced.


Lethal Enforcers is an on-the-rails lightgun game. The player is initially armed only with a standard issue revolver, but weapon upgrades such as a .357 Magnum, a shotgun and an automatic pistol can be collected by shooting at their on-screen counterparts as the game progresses. While some weapons can be reloaded, others can't and are only useful for a limited time. Any weapon upgrades are lost in the event of a player losing a life.


- TECHNICAL -


Game ID : GX191


Main CPU : HD6309 (@ 8 Mhz)

Sound CPU : Z80 (@ 8 Mhz)

