$info=volfied,volfiedu,volfiedj,
$bio

Volfied (c) 1989 Taito.


An update of Taito's 1981 classic, "Qix", Volfied adopts the same 'draw boxes to colour in the background' gameplay of its predessessor but updates both the graphics and in-game enemies. A number of power-ups are available, revealed when certain sections of the background have been filled, such as Speed-up, tempoaray enemy freeze and laser. The player's ship is only in danger from the game's enemies while the player is actually drawing a line. Each level must be completed within a tight time limit.


- TECHNICAL -


Prom Stickers : C04


Main CPU : 68000 (@ 8 Mhz), Z80 (@ 4 Mhz)

Sound Chips : YM2203 (@ 4 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Vertical

Video resolution : 240 x 320 pixels

Aspect ratio : 3/4

Screen refresh : 60.00 Hz

Palette colors : 8192


Players : 2

Control : 8-way joystick

Buttons : 1


